{
  "basis": "The routing criterion is to select the state with the highest prevalence from the dashboard. The dashboard's legend maps color to prevalence: pale yellow = high (≈100), dark burgundy = low (≈0). Georgia (GA) is colored dark burgundy, indicating the lowest prevalence category. Delaware (DE) is colored pale yellow, indicating the highest prevalence category. Rhode Island (RI) is gray, which is not mapped in the legend and thus cannot be assigned a prevalence rank. Therefore, Delaware (DE) is the only state with a clearly defined and highest prevalence value.",
  "option_label": "Open Delaware (DE) prevalence detail for routine monitoring"
}
